From: TB522FU Debian port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rotate TB522FU touch into landscape

Physical upper-left and upper-right taps map to native coordinates near
(maxX,0) and (maxX,maxY). Invert native X, then swap axes through the
standard touchscreen helpers already used by finger and pen reporting.
The display frame becomes 3840x2560. Real-input validation of the corrected
mapping remains required.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -454,6 +454,9 @@
 		firmware-name = "novatek_ts_38_new_fw.bin";
 		touchscreen-size-x = <2560>;
 		touchscreen-size-y = <3840>;
+		/* Native TL=(maxX,0), TR=(maxX,maxY): invert X before swap. */
+		touchscreen-inverted-x;
+		touchscreen-swapped-x-y;
 
 		novatek,pen-support;
 		novatek,spi-rd-fast-addr = <0>;
